# Build trees (one per CMake preset)
/build/
compile_commands.json
CMakeUserPresets.json

# vcpkg
/vcpkg_installed/

# Generated flatc headers live in the build tree only and are never committed
# (rule R3). Belt and braces in case someone points flatc at the source tree.
**/generated/

# Emscripten output
*.wasm
*.wasm.map

# Experiment output — CSVs are committed deliberately (see docs/EVALUATION.md),
# but scratch runs and rendered charts are not.
/results/scratch/
/results/**/*.png
/results/**/*.svg

# Generated scene assets (regenerated by script, never committed)
/assets/generated/

# Local coordinator state
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-shm

# Fuzzing artifacts. NOTE: fuzz/corpus/ is deliberately NOT ignored — seeds
# are committed evidence (docs/CONVENTIONS.md §7 T4, EVALUATION.md E8).
crash-*
leak-*
timeout-*
oom-*
/fuzz/artifacts/

# Secrets and local config
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# NOTE: do NOT add `*.md` here. An earlier revision did, which silently
# excluded CLAUDE.md, RESEARCH.md, and all of docs/ from version control —
# i.e. the entire handoff surface this repo depends on (RISKS.md R-E).

*.md
!README.md
results/
fuzz/dist/

# fuzz/corpus/ is deliberately NOT ignored. It IS the regression net: CI replays
# every committed seed with -runs=0 on each push, and R11 states outright that
# the corpus is committed.
#
# It was ignored until 2026-08-06, and 125 protocol seeds only existed in git
# because someone once force-added them. Every entry found since — 295 from the
# 4.12 campaign, plus the entire 4.13 asset corpus — was silently dropped, so
# CI's net was frozen at the original seeds while the logs reported half a
# billion executions. Same shape as the `*.md` mistake noted above: an ignore
# rule quietly excluding the thing it was protecting.